WEBVTT

00:00:00.018 --> 00:00:07.802
Prompting, fine-tuning, and RAG solve different problems, and choosing the wrong one can create unnecessary

00:00:07.802 --> 00:00:12.737
work. Prompting changes the instructions or examples given at inference time.

00:00:12.737 --> 00:00:20.587
It is useful when the model already has the capability you need but needs clearer guidance about format

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:24.682
or behavior. Fine-tuning changes model parameters using training data.

00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:29.537
It is useful when you need consistent task behavior, domain adaptation,

00:00:29.537 --> 00:00:33.817
or a specialized output pattern and have suitable examples.

00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:37.842
RAG does not primarily change the model weights.

00:00:37.842 --> 00:00:45.307
Instead, it retrieves external information at question time and places relevant evidence into the context.

00:00:45.307 --> 00:00:51.617
That is useful when answers depend on private, changing, or document-specific knowledge.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.162
These methods can also be combined.

00:00:54.162 --> 00:00:58.622
A fine-tuned or instruction-tuned model can still use RAG.

00:00:58.622 --> 00:01:04.599
The first question should always be: is the problem behavior, knowledge access, or both?
